# Tutorial: Save actions

Topic: `save_actions`

The file system tools `write_file` and `edit_file` have configurable save actions. These are commands that are executed after the file is written. They are configured in the file `.clawp_save_actions.yaml` in your workspace (i.e. you can change it).

The commands are executed in the file's directory and given the file name as an argument. If a command has an exit code other than 0, its output is appended to the tool result. By default, this is used to run formatting and linting for .py files, informing you if the file was formatted or there were linting errors.
